---
import Code from "./Code.astro";
import Wash from "./Wash.astro";
import { compareHaus, compareJson } from "@/content/samples";
---

<section class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 lg:py-32" aria-labelledby="compare-heading">
  <div class="max-w-[40rem]">
    <h2 id="compare-heading" class="text-[2.2rem] leading-[1.08] sm:text-[2.8rem]">The same data in JSON.</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-[1.12rem] text-ink-2">
      JSON can hold all of it, but only by convention: a <code class="inline-code">"type"</code> field for the
      status, plain strings for the date and the amount. Every team has to agree on those rules and write them
      down. In haus, they're <strong>part of the format</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="relative isolate mt-14 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-6">
    <Wash
      seed={8}
      class="-top-14 -left-14 -z-10 hidden h-[calc(100%+7rem)] w-[calc(50%+7rem)] md:block"
      strokes={[
        { x: 0.12, y: 0.18, rx: 0.13, ry: 0.18, color: "sap", strength: 0.9 },
        { x: 0.22, y: 0.08, rx: 0.12, ry: 0.09, color: "cerulean", strength: 0.75 },
        { x: 0.08, y: 0.62, rx: 0.07, ry: 0.1, color: "gold", strength: 0.85 },
      ]}
    />
    <Code code={compareHaus} lang="haus" label="order.haus" size="sm" />
    <Code code={compareJson} lang="json" label="order.json" size="sm" muted />
  </div>
</section>
